# dotfiles-arch

Rolling Arch / installed Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME workstation automation on x86_64/amd64: Kitty, tmux, Neovim, Claude Code,
Codex. Profiles are **additive multi-select** (`work`, `personal`, `devcontainer`).

## Orchestration

- `scripts/bootstrap.sh` (new machine) and `scripts/sync.sh` (drifted machine) both run
  a guarded upgrade → `scripts/run-profile-setup.sh` → `link-dotfiles.sh` → `post-link-hooks.sh`.
- Never duplicate the setup-script list; it lives only in `run-profile-setup.sh`.
- Detect hosts via the common header before mutation; disk provisioning and AUR-only utilities remain Arch-only.
- Use `native_package_installed` / `ensure_native_pkgs` for native packages and explicit app recipes for exceptions. Sources/update owners: [PACKAGES.md](../../PACKAGES.md).
- Required failures reach final status; successful update stamps follow all requested update owners. Cleanup previews until separately authorized with a terminal and typing `remove`; `--yes` is insufficient.
- Preserve foreign config files/links, driver flavor, managed agents, holds/pins and automatic security updates.
- Dotfiles link through installed `~/.local/share/workstation/config` generations. Source edits use verified `dfa-deploy source`; deployment/migration/recovery policy: [docs/deployment.md](../../docs/deployment.md).

## Paths and config

- Use `USER_HOME_DIR` (from `dotheader.sh`), never a hardcoded `/home/<user>`.
- Read and write saved settings only through `load_bootstrap_config` /
  `write_bootstrap_config` — never hand-edit `~/.config/dotfiles-arch/.dotfiles_bootstrap_config`.
- Keys: `FULL_NAME`, `EMAIL_ADDRESS`, `SETUP_PROFILES` (space-separated multi-select),
  `SETUP_PROFILE` (primary, for older readers / Super+B preference), `INSTALL_NVIDIA`,
  `MACHINE_TYPE`, `DEFAULT_HARNESS` (legacy `DEFAULT_AGENT` migrates through the accessor).
- Profile helpers: `has_setup_profile`, `normalize_setup_profiles`, `primary_setup_profile`.
- `MACHINE_TYPE` is `laptop|desktop` and drives power policy in `setup-gnome.sh`
  (`power-profiles-daemon`, the logind lid drop-in — laptop: suspend on battery,
  ignore lid on AC/docked — USB HID wake udev rules, audio powersave). Fall back to
  `machine_is_laptop` / `has_battery` when it is unset.

## Security

- AUR installs go through `ensure_yay_pkgs` / `ensure_yay_installed`, which IoC-scan
  PKGBUILDs (and AUR deps) first. Do not bypass them with raw `yay -S`.
- Do not add `curl | bash` installers. Download to a temp file and verify a checksum,
  or use a repo/AUR package.

